# Every route of server.py, for the REST Client extension (humao.rest-client).
# Start the server first: uv run uvicorn server:app --port 8000
# Click "Send Request" above a request.
#
# Create a session, copy the "id" from the response, and replace SESSION_ID in the URLs below.
# Copy ARTIFACT_ID from the artifacts list.
#
# This extension cannot show a stream, so subscribe to events in a terminal instead:
#   curl -N http://127.0.0.1:8000/sessions/SESSION_ID/events

### Create a session (POST /sessions)
POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/sessions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "message": "Use get_customer to tell me customer 123's plan."
}

### List sessions (GET /sessions)
GET http://127.0.0.1:8000/sessions?limit=5

### Get one session: status and pending actions (GET /sessions/{id})
GET http://127.0.0.1:8000/sessions/SESSION_ID

### Update reasoning effort: low, medium or high (PATCH /sessions/{id})
PATCH http://127.0.0.1:8000/sessions/SESSION_ID
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "effort": "low"
}

### Saved history (GET /sessions/{id}/items)
GET http://127.0.0.1:8000/sessions/SESSION_ID/items

### Send a message (POST /sessions/{id}/messages)
# Sending again with the same Idempotency-Key is treated as a retry, not a new message.
POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/sessions/SESSION_ID/messages
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: my-first-message

{
  "text": "Tell me customer 123's plan."
}

### Cancel the running turn (POST /sessions/{id}/cancel)
POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/sessions/SESSION_ID/cancel

### Stream events (GET /sessions/{id}/events)
# Not sent from here. Run in a terminal: curl -N http://127.0.0.1:8000/sessions/SESSION_ID/events

### Delete the session (DELETE /sessions/{id})
DELETE http://127.0.0.1:8000/sessions/SESSION_ID

### Upload a file into the hosted workspace (POST /sessions/{id}/files)
POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/sessions/SESSION_ID/files
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "path": "/workspace/notes.txt",
  "text": "Course verified\n"
}

### Ask the agent to write a file that becomes an artifact
POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/sessions/SESSION_ID/messages
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "text": "Copy /workspace/notes.txt to /workspace/outputs/notes.txt."
}

### List artifacts and copy an artifact "id" (GET /sessions/{id}/artifacts)
GET http://127.0.0.1:8000/sessions/SESSION_ID/artifacts

### Download an artifact (GET /sessions/{id}/artifacts/{artifact_id})
GET http://127.0.0.1:8000/sessions/SESSION_ID/artifacts/ARTIFACT_ID
